msgid "Configuring Logging"
msgstr ""

msgid "This guide explains logging and how to configure it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Internally, Quarkus uses JBoss Log Manager and the JBoss Logging facade.\n"
"You can use the JBoss Logging facade inside your code as it's already "
"provided,\n"
"or any of the supported Logging API listed in the next chapter as Quarkus "
"will send them to JBoss Log Manager."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the logging configuration will then be done inside your `application."
"properties`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Supported Logging APIs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Applications and components may use any of the following APIs for logging, "
"and the logs will be merged:"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK `java.util.logging` (also called JUL)"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://github.com/jboss-logging/jboss-logging[JBoss Logging]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://www.slf4j.org/[SLF4J]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-logging/[Apache Commons Logging]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Internally Quarkus uses JBoss Logging; you can also use it inside your "
"application so that no other dependencies should be added for your logs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging with Panache"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead of declaring a `Logger` field, you can use the simplified logging "
"API:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `io.quarkus.logging.Log` class mirrors the JBoss Logging API, except all "
"methods are `static`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that the class doesn't declare a logger field.\n"
"This is because during application build, a `private static final org.jboss."
"logging.Logger` field is created automatically, in each class that uses the "
"`Log` API.\n"
"The fully qualified name of the class that calls the `Log` methods is used "
"as a logger name.\n"
"In this example, the logger name would be `com.example.MyService`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Finally, during application build, all calls to `Log` methods are rewritten "
"to regular JBoss Logging calls on the logger field."
msgstr ""

msgid "Injecting a Logger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also inject a configured `org.jboss.logging.Logger` instance in your "
"beans and resource classes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The FQCN of the declaring class is used as a logger name, i.e. `org.jboss."
"logging.Logger.getLogger(SimpleBean.class)` will be used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, the name _foo_ is used as a logger name, i.e. `org.jboss."
"logging.Logger.getLogger(\"foo\")` will be used."
msgstr ""

msgid "What about Apache Log4j ?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/[Log4j] is a logging "
"implementation: it contains a logging backend and a logging facade.\n"
"Quarkus uses the JBoss Log Manager backend, so you will need to include the "
"`log4j2-jboss-logmanager` library to route Log4j logs to JBoss Log Manager."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is the library needed for Log4j version 2; if you use the legacy Log4j "
"version 1 you need to use `log4j-jboss-logmanager` instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can then use the Log4j API inside your application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging levels"
msgstr ""

msgid "These are the log levels used by Quarkus:"
msgstr ""

msgid "OFF"
msgstr ""

msgid "Special level to turn off logging."
msgstr ""

msgid "FATAL"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A critical service failure/complete inability to service requests of any "
"kind."
msgstr ""

msgid "ERROR"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A significant disruption in a request or the inability to service a request."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARN"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A non-critical service error or problem that may not require immediate "
"correction."
msgstr ""

msgid "INFO"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Service lifecycle events or important related very-low-frequency information."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "DEBUG"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Messages that convey extra information regarding lifecycle or non-request-"
"bound events which may be helpful for debugging."
msgstr ""

msgid "TRACE"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Messages that convey extra per-request debugging information that may be "
"very high frequency."
msgstr ""

msgid "ALL"
msgstr ""

msgid "Special level for all messages including custom levels."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In addition, the following levels may be configured for applications and "
"libraries using link:https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/"
"logging/Level.html[`java.util.logging`]:"
msgstr ""

msgid "SEVERE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **ERROR**."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARNING"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **WARN**."
msgstr ""

msgid "CONFIG"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service configuration information."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **DEBUG**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINER"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **TRACE**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINEST"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Event more debugging information than `TRACE`, maybe with even higher "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

msgid "Runtime configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Run time logging is configured in the `application.properties` file,\n"
"for example, to set the default log level to `INFO` logging and include "
"Hibernate `DEBUG` logs:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting a log level below `DEBUG` requires the minimum log level to be "
"adjusted,\n"
"either globally via the `quarkus.log.min-level` property or per-category as "
"shown in the example above,\n"
"as well as adjusting the log level itself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Minimum logging level sets a floor level that Quarkus will be needed to "
"potentially generate,\n"
"opening the door to optimization opportunities.\n"
"As an example, in native execution the minimum level enables lower level "
"checks (e.g. `isTraceEnabled`) to be folded to `false`,\n"
"resulting in dead code elimination for code that will never to be executed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All possible properties are listed in <<loggingConfigurationReference, the "
"logging configuration reference>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging categories"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Logging is done on a per-category basis.  Each category can be independently "
"configured.\n"
"A configuration which applies to a category will also apply to all sub-"
"categories of that category,\n"
"unless there is a more specific matching sub-category configuration.\n"
"For every category the same settings that are configured on ( console / file "
"/ syslog ) apply.\n"
"These can also be overridden by attaching a one or more named handlers to a "
"category. See example in <<category-named-handlers-example>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Property Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"INFO footnote:[Some extensions may define customized default log levels for "
"certain categories, in order to reduce log noise by default.  Setting the "
"log level in configuration will override any extension-defined log levels.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The level to use to configure the category named `<category-name>`.  The "
"quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The minimum logging level to use to configure the category named `<category-"
"name>`.  The quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".use-parent-handlers"
msgstr ""

msgid "true"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify whether this logger should send its output to its parent logger."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".handlers=[<handler>]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"empty footnote:[By default, the configured category gets the same handlers "
"attached as the one on the root logger.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The names of the handlers that you want to attach to a specific category."
msgstr ""

msgid "Root logger configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The root logger category is handled separately, and is configured via the "
"following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default minimum log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If no level configuration exists for a given logger category, the enclosing "
"(parent) category is examined. If no categories are configured which enclose "
"the category in question, then the root logger configuration is used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging Format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Quarkus uses a pattern-based logging formatter that generates "
"human-readable text logs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can configure the format for each log handler via a dedicated property.\n"
"For the console handler, the property is `quarkus.log.console.format`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The logging format string supports the following symbols:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Symbol"
msgstr ""

msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid "%%"
msgstr ""

msgid "`%`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders a simple `%` character."
msgstr ""

msgid "%c"
msgstr ""

msgid "Category"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the category name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%C"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source class"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source class name.footnote:calc[Format sequences which examine "
"caller information may affect performance]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%d{xxx}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Date"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders a date with the given date format string, which uses the syntax "
"defined by `java.text.SimpleDateFormat`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%e"
msgstr ""

msgid "Exception"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the thrown exception, if any."
msgstr ""

msgid "%F"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source file name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%h"
msgstr ""

msgid "Host name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the system simple host name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%H"
msgstr ""

msgid "Qualified host name"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the system's fully qualified host name, which may be the same as the "
"simple host name, depending on OS configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "%i"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process ID"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the current process PID."
msgstr ""

msgid "%l"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source location"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source location information, which includes source file name, "
"line number, class name, and method name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%L"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source line number.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%m"
msgstr ""

msgid "Full Message"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the log message plus exception (if any)."
msgstr ""

msgid "%M"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source method"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source method name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%n"
msgstr ""

msgid "Newline"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the platform-specific line separator string."
msgstr ""

msgid "%N"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the name of the current process."
msgstr ""

msgid "%p"
msgstr ""

msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the log level of the message."
msgstr ""

msgid "%r"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Render the time in milliseconds since the start of the application log."
msgstr ""

msgid "%s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Simple message"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders just the log message, with no exception trace."
msgstr ""

msgid "%t"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thread name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the thread name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%t{id}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thread ID"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the thread ID."
msgstr ""

msgid "%z{<zone name>}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Time zone"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set the time zone of the output to `<zone name>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%X{<MDC property name>}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mapped Diagnostics Context Value"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the value from Mapped Diagnostics Context"
msgstr ""

msgid "%X"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mapped Diagnostics Context Values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Mapped Diagnostics Context in format {property."
"key=property.value}"
msgstr ""

msgid "%x"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested Diagnostics context values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Nested Diagnostics Context in format {value1."
"value2}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Alternative Console Logging Formats"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is possible to change the output format of the console log. This can be "
"useful in environments where the output\n"
"of the Quarkus application is captured by a service which can, for example, "
"process and store the log information for\n"
"later analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "JSON Logging Format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order to configure the JSON logging format, the `quarkus-logging-json` "
"extension may be employed.\n"
"Add this extension to your build file as the following snippet illustrates:"
